proach is limited by the lack of shared vocabularies for conditions of use, user qualifications, legal constraints, and similar important items. ODRL is thus limited to describing policies in terms of the disseminating institution, but provides a basis for expansion in future when the needed vocabularies are developed.","position":{"start":{"line":29,"column":1},"end":{"line":29,"column":1}},"key":"fS0PLxYQ8U"}],"key":"azg83JqJlF"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":31,"column":1},"end":{"line":31,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"link","url":"https://cross-domain-interoperability-framework.github.io/cdifbook/controlled-vocabularies/conceptprofile/","position":{"start":{"line":31,"column":1},"end":{"line":31,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"strong","position":{"start":{"line":31,"column":1},"end":{"line":31,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Concept Scheme Profile","position":{"start":{"line":31,"column":1},"end":{"line":31,"column":1}},"key":"znu5rxOIeC"}],"key":"Jte6mvQHB4"}],"urlSource":"https://cross-domain-interoperability-framework.github.io/cdifbook/controlled-vocabularies/conceptprofile/","key":"wwGovm5uqh"},{"type":"text","value":": This profile recommends the use of ","position":{"start":{"line":31,"column":1},"end":{"line":31,"column":1}},"key":"WegZYkrkvN"},{"type":"link","url":"https://www.w3.org/TR/2009/REC-skos-reference-20090818/","position":{"start":{"line":31,"column":1},"end":{"line":31,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"SKOS","position":{"start":{"line":31,"column":1},"end":{"line":31,"column":1}},"key":"Qef6WjkF6Z"}],"urlSource":"https://www.w3.org/TR/2009/REC-skos-reference-20090818/","key":"trV6UyhQOU"},{"type":"text","value":" for describing controlled vocabularies, understood to mean any terminological resource. The use of ","position":{"start":{"line":31,"column":1},"end":{"line":31,"column":1}},"key":"oboJceqaPk"},{"type":"link","url":"https://www.w3.org/TR/owl2-overview/","position":{"start":{"line":31,"column":1},"end":{"line":31,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"OWL","position":{"start":{"line":31,"column":1},"end":{"line":31,"column":1}},"key":"P9JL3xkU4Y"}],"urlSource":"https://www.w3.org/TR/owl2-overview/","key":"RO7Y2WDkIW"},{"type":"text","value":" as a linked extension towhat is presented in SKOS is also recommended, as is the use of ","position":{"start":{"line":31,"column":1},"end":{"line":31,"column":1}},"key":"aN6QlmHwdh"},{"type":"link","url":"https://ddialliance.org/Specification/RDF/XKOS","position":{"start":{"line":31,"column":1},"end":{"line":31,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"XKOS","position":{"start":{"line":31,"column":1},"end":{"line":31,"column":1}},"key":"HnQXFsAe5q"}],"urlSource":"https://ddialliance.org/Specification/RDF/XKOS","key":"PEoOmdY4QP"},{"type":"text","value":" for formal statistical classifications.","position":{"start":{"line":31,"column":1},"end":{"line":31,"column":1}},"key":"bCSUYi6mf1"}],"key":"FhvJvhpWkP"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":33,"column":1},"end":{"line":33,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"link","url":"https://cross-domain-interoperability-framework.github.io/cdifbook/data-description/datadescriptionprofile/","position":{"start":{"line":33,"column":1},"end":{"line":33,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"strong","position":{"start":{"line":33,"column":1},"end":{"line":33,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Data Description Profile","position":{"start":{"line":33,"column":1},"end":{"line":33,"column":1}},"key":"xTu2BktiT1"}],"key":"a5viSPKpI0"}],"urlSource":"https://cross-domain-interoperability-framework.github.io/cdifbook/data-description/datadescriptionprofile/","key":"DkWiaR61ag"},{"type":"text","value":": This profile recommends the use of ","position":{"start":{"line":33,"column":1},"end":{"line":33,"column":1}},"key":"If7Tajf6XS"},{"type":"link","url":"https://schema.org","position":{"start":{"line":33,"column":1},"end":{"line":33,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Schema.org","position":{"start":{"line":33,"column":1},"end":{"line":33,"column":1}},"key":"uCcyn9zd3r"}],"urlSource":"https://schema.org","key":"e4agp0hkEm"},{"type":"text","value":" and ","position":{"start":{"line":33,"column":1},"end":{"line":33,"column":1}},"key":"wJ0qQBOrmZ"},{"type":"link","url":"https://ddialliance.org/Specification/ddi-cdi","position":{"start":{"line":33,"column":1},"end":{"line":33,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"DDI-CDI","position":{"start":{"line":33,"column":1},"end":{"line":33,"column":1}},"key":"wkyplQnRln"}],"urlSource":"https://ddialliance.org/Specification/ddi-cdi","key":"fYeFIPn3q2"},{"type":"text","value":" to provide a granular description of quantitative data sets, and how the logical content of those datasets relates to their physical encoding. Both text-based (i.e., CSV, fixed-width) and binary (i.e., NetCDF, HDF5, Parquet) are supported. The recommendations cover description of individual data sets to make them ‘integration-ready’.","position":{"start":{"line":33,"column":1},"end":{"line":33,"column":1}},"key":"hbcWBmQJEI"}],"key":"r8T8H0QmO2"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":35,"column":1},"end":{"line":35,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"link","url":"https://cross-domain-interoperability-framework.github.io/cdifbook/controlled-vocabularies/codelistprofile/","position":{"start":{"line":35,"column":1},"end":{"line":35,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"strong","position":{"start":{"line":35,"column":1},"end":{"line":35,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Codelist Profile","position":{"start":{"line":35,"column":1},"end":{"line":35,"column":1}},"key":"tE1DXTXBLI"}],"key":"MpmCk5Owqm"}],"urlSource":"https://cross-domain-interoperability-framework.github.io/cdifbook/controlled-vocabularies/codelistprofile/","key":"KugWUf8dnp"},{"type":"text","value":": This profile recommends the use of ","position":{"start":{"line":35,"column":1},"end":{"line":35,"column":1}},"key":"KAfWNwSUPK"},{"type":"link","url":"https://www.w3.org/TR/2009/REC-skos-reference-20090818/","position":{"start":{"line":35,"column":1},"end":{"line":35,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"SKOS","position":{"start":{"line":35,"column":1},"end":{"line":35,"column":1}},"key":"htZEywmLyi"}],"urlSource":"https://www.w3.org/TR/2009/REC-skos-reference-20090818/","key":"oHNt2fkV2L"},{"type":"text","value":" for describing the enumerated sets of values used to populate the fields in data sets. These are used in the description of data sets and their structures in the Data Description and Data Structure profiles.","position":{"start":{"line":35,"column":1},"end":{"line":35,"column":1}},"key":"g5WTddFpiw"}],"key":"OGnJk3fQoL"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":37,"column":1},"end":{"line":37,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"link","url":"https://cross-domain-interoperability-framework.github.io/cdifbook/data-description/datastructureprofile/","position":{"start":{"line":37,"column":1},"end":{"line":37,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"strong","position":{"start":{"line":37,"column":1},"end":{"line":37,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Data Structure Profile","position":{"start":{"line":37,"column":1},"end":{"line":37,"column":1}},"key":"brxHvxHsMY"}],"key":"g3z3iiSqKK"}],"urlSource":"https://cross-domain-interoperability-framework.github.io/cdifbook/data-description/datastructureprofile/","key":"ErTBDTKJ3m"},{"type":"text","value":": This profile uses ","position":{"start":{"line":37,"column":1},"end":{"line":37,"column":1}},"key":"zuPkR1kMMk"},{"type":"link","url":"https://ddialliance.org/Specification/ddi-cdi","position":{"start":{"line":37,"column":1},"end":{"line":37,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"DDI-CDI","position":{"start":{"line":37,"column":1},"end":{"line":37,"column":1}},"key":"PKUrrb2COS"}],"urlSource":"https://ddialliance.org/Specification/ddi-cdi","key":"wnzJCVccye"},{"type":"text","value":" to describe reusable data structures and variables. In future, this capaility will be extended to data formats.","position":{"start":{"line":37,"column":1},"end":{"line":37,"column":1}},"key":"TWhDQVniia"}],"key":"O8pgGRs0nw"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":39,"column":1},"end":{"line":39,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"link","url":"https://cross-domain-interoperability-framework.github.io/cdifbook/universals/univintro/","position":{"start":{"line":39,"column":1},"end":{"line":39,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"strong","position":{"start":{"line":39,"column":1},"end":{"line":39,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Universals Profile","position":{"start":{"line":39,"column":1},"end":{"line":39,"column":1}},"key":"dnKPDdSOYH"}],"key":"NA3LQsDDiN"}],"urlSource":"https://cross-domain-interoperability-framework.github.io/cdifbook/universals/univintro/","key":"wBqe2uomyt"},{"type":"text","value":": This section recommends the information which should be provided when describingtime, geography, and units of measurement in other metadata sets. Some standards for this purpose arerecommended in each area.","position":{"start":{"line":39,"column":1},"end":{"line":39,"column":1}},"key":"o8j5pPVh5F"}],"key":"E50XQU7w8T"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":42,"column":1},"end":{"line":42,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"The CDIF includes recommendation for specific implementation approaches in each profile, based on web technology. While many standards and vocabularies require the use of RDF, it is not a technology that is commonly used in every domain. The solution to this is to advocate the use of JSON-LD, which allows the expression of RDF vocabularies in the common JSON syntax.","position":{"start":{"line":42,"column":1},"end":{"line":42,"column":1}},"key":"TsJKT5i6cG"}],"key":"xRtiktFgUC"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":44,"column":1},"end":{"line":44,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"In each profile a minimum set of required fields are specified to support common cases. Other optional fields are suggested, and the path forward toward support of more complex scenarios is indicated. While FAIR implementation is demanding, it is hoped that consistent use of a common core of metadata can minimize the effort required.","position":{"start":{"line":44,"column":1},"end":{"line":44,"column":1}},"key":"CIGbIZnjpo"}],"key":"BNYLiDkDsG"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":46,"column":1},"end":{"line":46,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Users only need adopt those profiles that are useful to them. There is no requirement for the adoption of optional profile content. For example, it is possible to describe data to make it ‘integration ready’ at a detailed level, but not to support profiles for data discovery or access, to give but one example. CDIF profiles are intended to be a toolkit for implementation, with the needed functions being addressed in any specific setting according to implementer priorities.","position":{"start":{"line":46,"column":1},"end":{"line":46,"column":1}},"key":"ch8jR4fVYf"}],"key":"xnNdKtFGoh"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":48,"column":1},"end":{"line":48,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"For some common combinations of profiles, implementation artefacts will also be provided as a convenience.","position":{"start":{"line":48,"column":1},"end":{"line":48,"column":1}},"key":"RlbjTEfAhl"}],"key":"Tqh1za9M5w"}],"key":"qK82tNtz3q"}],"key":"VMykoRwXcC"},"references":{"cite":{"order":[],"data":{}}},"footer":{"navigation":{"prev":{"title":"Why CDIF Matters","url":"/background/whycdif","group":"Overview"},"next":{"title":"Conformance with the CDIF Guidelines","url":"/background/conformance","group":"Overview"}}},"domain":"http://localhost:3000"}